===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# To provide with pillars or added strength as if from pillars.
#* {{quote-book|title=Blast furnace practice|author=James Morgan|year=1910|passage=Insufficient penetration, or faulty distribution of the blast, may give rise to "'''pillaring'''" — that is, the formation of a pillar or column of cold material extending up through the middle of the hearth}}
#* {{quote-book|title=First annual Symposium on Frontiers of Engineering|page=25|author=National Academy of Engineering|year=1996|passage=We discovered this new class of compounds in our search for a means of generating porosity by '''pillaring''' layered double hydroxides}}
#* {{quote-book|title=Functional and smart materials|page=226|author=|Zhong Lin Wang|co-authors=Zhen Chuan Kang|year=1998|passage=In the pillaring-grafting reaction the dimensionality increases by '''pillaring''' the organic or precursory polynuclear metal hydroxyl cations into an inorganic layer structured matrix.}}
#* {{quote-book|title=Handbook of layered materials|page=261|author=Scott M. Auerbach|coauthors=Kathleen A. Carrado, Prabir K. Dutta|year=2004|passage=It was then that scientists started to create porosity in the interlayer space of layered clays. developing the first '''pillared''' clays with pores in the larger microporous region.}}

